{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfiHu1KSBEoJ3kCHXTXDy", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "```\nTable 3 reports the estimates, and identity matters. In column 2, the coefficient on the identity-disclosed indicator is 0.18 (SE = 0.04). It holds up in column 3, where adding product fixed effects leaves it at 0.15 (SE = 0.05). The interaction with reviewer tenure, 0.09 (SE = 0.03) in column 4, shows that the effect of disclosure grows with tenure. Star rating remains a strong driver of sales, with a coefficient of 0.42 (SE = 0.02) across all specifications, yet identity adds to it. R-squared rises from 0.31 to 0.47 across the columns. All coefficients are significant at the 1% level except the interaction, which is significant at the 5% level.\n```\n\nTwo notes on the edits. First, I added a few interpretive phrases (\"identity matters,\" \"holds up,\" \"grows with tenure\") that go slightly beyond your original wording; the \"grows with tenure\" reading assumes a positive interaction means the disclosure effect strengthens with tenure, so cut it if you'd rather leave interpretation to the discussion section. Second, I kept every number, SE, and significance level exactly as you had them, and there were no citations to preserve."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1659, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1391, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1659}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "67a85a5c-5528-50ca-a038-89c6a50acf16", "uuid": "8300c670-bc39-4994-bb7e-a1909c642b5f", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T02:21:25.055Z", "request_id": "req_011CfiHu16oGFdS9RFU6Zjur"}
